OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Mon 5 Oct to Wed 14 OctFThe
OL,6,Fsouthern UK will likely be under the
OL,7,Finfluence of high pressure for the
OL,8,Ffirst few days of this period. This
OL,9,Fmeans plenty of dry weather to be had
OL,10,Fhere, albeit with some chilly nights
OL,11,Fand overnight and morning fog in
OL,12,Fplaces. In the north, a rather more
OL,13,Fchangeable pattern will continue, with
OL,14,Foccasional rain and windy conditions
OL,15,Fat times. Broadly changeable weather
OL,16,Fpatterns look to continue through mid-
OL,17,Fmonth, with ridges of high pressure
OL,18,Fextending from the southwest,
OL,19,Finterspersed by Atlantic frontal
OL,20,Fsystems. These could be associated
OL,21,Fwith quite deep and fast-moving
OL,22,Fdepressions, bringing the potential
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Ffor windy weather more widely, again
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fmost likely in the north. Temperatures
OL,25,Fprobably near or slightly above normal
OL,26,Foverall, with day to day variations.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
